# Documentation (`docs/content/`)

The documentation is built from `docs/`: a Nuxt 4 application with the Docus
layer, which renders the markdown in `docs/content/` through Nuxt Content (MDC
syntax for components) and Nuxt UI; the few own components are Vue single-file
components in `docs/app/components/`. The same content is printed to the PDF
manuals. How it is built, where the images come from and how the version badge
and the "Last updated" line work is described in `docs/README.md`.

| Section | Folder | Content |
|---------|--------|---------|
| User manual | `docs/content/1.manual/` | The complete reference for pilots |
| Quick guide | `docs/content/2.quick-guide/` | The shortest path from installation to the first flights |
| InfoBox reference | `docs/content/3.infobox/` | One page per InfoBox, see below |
| Hardware | `docs/content/4.hardware/` | Devices XCSoar runs on and connects to |
| Developers | `docs/content/5.dev/` | Building, hacking on and contributing to XCSoar |

The rules in **Files and frontmatter**, **Text conventions** and
**Components** apply to all five sections.

## When to update

If a change is **user-visible** (new or changed UI, setting, InfoBox, menu,
gesture, file format a pilot uses, installation step), update the **English**
user manual in `docs/content/1.manual/` (not `docs/content/5.dev/`) and add a
`NEWS.txt` bullet under `* documentation` (see `.cursor/rules/news.txt.mdc`).
A new or changed InfoBox also updates `docs/content/3.infobox/`, see below.

Do **not** update the user manual for pure refactors, CI, or developer-only
APIs; those belong in `docs/content/5.dev/` and under `* development` in
`NEWS.txt`. There are no translations in `docs/`; do not translate.

